BT /B 9 Tf 333.0709 70.8661 Td (START  25.5 cm2  -  recommended first) Tj ET
BT /R 6.5 Tf 333.0709 58.1102 Td (luff 110.8 mm  /  foot 46.0 mm  /  grey and navy = sail detail, cut on the black line) Tj ET
BT /B 6 Tf 350.6457 430.1575 Td (HEAD) Tj ET
BT /B 6 Tf 333.0709 97.7953 Td (TACK) Tj ET
BT /B 6 Tf 439.4835 97.7953 Td (CLEW) Tj ET
BT /R 6.5 Tf 333.0709 86.4567 Td (clew -> 3rd hole from the boom end \(46 mm aft of mast\)) Tj ET
BT /B 11 Tf 317.4803 717.1654 Td (How to fit) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 697.3228 Td (1. Laminate with MATTE clear tape on both faces \(keeps the grey seams\).) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 682.5827 Td (2. Pierce the marked holes with a pin, then open to ~1 mm.) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 667.8425 Td (3. Head: thread through the tab hole. Full sail: tie to the) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 653.1024 Td (    masthead hole. Start / medium: tie round the mast just) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 638.3622 Td (    ABOVE the upper spreader \(the spreader stops it sliding\).) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 623.6220 Td (4. Luff: small thread loops through each luff hole and round) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 608.8819 Td (    the mast. Keep loops off the spreader roots \(dashed marks\).) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 594.1417 Td (5. Tack: lash round the mast just above the boom.) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 579.4016 Td (6. Clew: tie down to the matching boom hole; snug, not tight.) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 564.6614 Td (7. Sheet: tie a thread to the boom sheet hole, run it down through) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 549.9213 Td (    the coachroof sheet eye, set the boom ~15 deg off centre, tie off.) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 535.1811 Td (The printed shroud frame holds the mast; the paper only drives.) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 520.4409 Td () Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 505.7008 Td (Markings: MGT 43 reads from port; the mirrored, higher set reads) Tj ET
BT /R 7.2 Tf 317.4803 490.9606 Td (    from starboard through the taped paper, as on a real main.) Tj ET
